<BaseLayout title="NodeX | Faisal Ahmed Khan" description="NodeX is a planned AI-assisted circuit analysis and learning platform.">
  <header class="page-header"><p class="eyebrow">Project · In progress / planned</p><h1>NodeX</h1><p>AI-Assisted Circuit Analysis &amp; Learning Platform</p></header>
  <article class="prose">
    <h2>Overview</h2><p>NodeX is a planned learning and circuit-analysis tool intended to help users understand and analyze electrical circuits, including AC/DC analysis and equivalent circuits.</p>
    <h2>Problem</h2><p>Circuit analysis can be difficult to learn when a learner needs both a correct process and a clear explanation of why each step is used. NodeX is intended to support that learning journey.</p>
    <h2>Goals &amp; intended users</h2><p>The project is aimed at learners who want to study circuit-analysis concepts more clearly. Its intended goals are to support learning around AC/DC circuit analysis and equivalent-circuit ideas.</p>
    <h2>Technology</h2><p class="notice">The implementation technology has not been published or verified yet. No AI, analysis engine, interface, or feature is claimed as complete on this page.</p>
    <h2>Current status</h2><p>NodeX is in the planning and development stage. The concept and intended scope are defined, while the implementation status of individual features has not been documented publicly.</p>
    <h2>Next steps</h2><ul><li>Refine the learning and circuit-analysis scope.</li><li>Document the selected technical approach when verified.</li><li>Record implemented features, limitations, and learning outcomes as development progresses.</li></ul>
